    "response_text": "[{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Analyzing Instruction Types**\\n\\nI'm currently refining my understanding of how instructions are represented, differentiating between literal values and actual string data. This distinction is crucial as I move forward with analyzing the binary's obfuscation techniques, particularly within the `evaluate` function.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Unpacking Obfuscation Logic**\\n\\nI'm focusing on how subroutines manipulate the stack and alter return addresses to bypass static analysis. The `evaluate` function's digit parsing logic is key, and understanding these control flow obfuscation techniques is critical.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Analyzing Control Flow**\\n\\nI'm currently dissecting the obfuscation, identifying \\\"Jumping over junk\\\" via return address modification, likely from an LLVM pass. My focus is on understanding how this impacts the control flow and any opaque predicates.\\n\\n**Refining Function Computation**\\n\\nI am now clarifying the precise integer computation of the `evaluate` function from its string input, and will detail the control-flow alterations made by the obfuscator.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Investigating String Parsing**\\n\\nI'm now scrutinizing the `evaluate` function's memory to pinpoint operations related to character parsing and arithmetic. My goal is to confirm if it's a simple `atoi`-like function or a more complex expression parser by examining instructions like `SUB EAX, 0x30` and searching for multiplication routines.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Parsing Expression Inputs**\\n\\nI'm currently re-examining the `evaluate` function, questioning my initial assumption of a simple `atoi`. The \\\"usage\\\" string strongly suggests it parses an expression, and I need to investigate for operators that would indicate a more complex parser rather than a simple integer conversion.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Finding Call-Stack Tampering**\\n\\nI'm now observing how return addresses on the stack are being modified, specifically with additions like `0x17` or `0x15`. This, combined with junk instructions after calls, strongly suggests a call-stack tampering obfuscation technique.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Deconstructing Obfuscation Techniques**\\n\\nI'm now focusing on how return addresses are patched and junk code is inserted to thwart disassembly. Helper subroutines are being used to delegate operations, complicating the analysis of the primary function's logic.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Analyzing Junk Instruction Patterns**\\n\\nI'm focusing on how junk instructions following calls cause static analysis tools to fail disassembly. This appears to be a deliberate tactic to obscure control flow, especially when combined with return address modifications within helper functions.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Parsing Digit-by-Digit**\\n\\nI'm currently analyzing the `evaluate` function, and it appears to be parsing digit by digit from an expression string. While the specific arithmetic operators are obscured due to control flow obfuscation, I'm confirming the core logic involves converting characters to integers, similar to an `atoi` function.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Revisiting Expression Parsing**\\n\\nI'm now re-evaluating the `evaluate` function from the start, scrutinizing memory allocations and register usage. It appears I overlooked some key initialization steps in a helper function related to `[RBP-14h]` and `[RBP-18h]`, which might be crucial for correctly parsing the expression string.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Dissecting Expression Evaluation**\\n\\nI'm analyzing how the `evaluate` function processes expression strings character by character, converting digits and handling arithmetic. My current focus is on confirming the exact integer computations and identifying the operators used to parse the expression, despite the control flow obfuscation.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Clarifying Helper Function Interactions**\\n\\nI'm now detailing how helper functions, specifically `FUN_00102163` and `FUN_001022d6`, manage stack operations for local initialization and argument retrieval. My focus is on how they modify return addresses to bypass static analysis by injecting junk code after calls.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Verifying Expression Parsing**\\n\\nI'm now reconfirming that the `evaluate` function handles simple arithmetic expressions, not just integer conversion. My analysis of the \\\"usage\\\" string and the need to account for operators, despite the obscured control flow, confirms this broader parsing capability.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Reconstructing Expression Logic**\\n\\nI'm currently rebuilding the expression evaluation logic from scratch, integrating the observed digit-by-digit parsing and arithmetic operations. My focus is on mapping the transformed control flow to a coherent execution path, thereby revealing the underlying expression parsing mechanism.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"**Adding Junk Instructions**\\n\\nI'm now verifying that junk instructions are consistently present in the prologue and after calls, performing meaningless arithmetic. I've confirmed specific examples of these dead operations interleaving legitimate code.\\n\\n\",\"thought\":true}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"functionCall\":{\"name\":\"update_topic\",\"args\":{\"title\":\"Synthesizing Analysis and Findings\",\"summary\":\"I completed the raw memory tracing and string analysis, identifying that the obfuscation heavily utilizes return-address patching and junk code insertion to break CFG recovery. I have reconstructed the behavior of the 'evaluate' function and the roles of its subroutines. I am now preparing the final comprehensive report addressing all the user's tasks.\",\"strategic_intent\":\"I have gathered sufficient information to explain the binary's logic and obfuscation. I am now transitioning to compiling the final answer based on the analysis of evaluate, FUN_00102163, and FUN_001022d6.\"},\"id\":\"update_topic__call_12737836125391139903\"},\"thoughtSignature\":\"\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"STOP\"}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"promptTokenCount\":38901,\"candidatesTokenCount\":155,\"totalTokenCount\":44483,\"cachedContentTokenCount\":30809,\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\",\"promptTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":38901}],\"cacheTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":30809}],\"candidatesTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":155}],\"thoughtsTokenCount\":5427},\"responseId\":\"v90Ea8MWz4vq2Q_--sXhAw\",\"model